.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt OPEN 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm open
.Nd open files, folders and applications
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl e | Fl t | Fl a Ar application | Fl b Ar bundle-id
.Op Fl R
.Op Fl n
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens each
.Ar file
with the application that opens its kind of file, as a double click in
Argos does: folders open in Argos, applications are launched, documents go
to their application (launched if it is not running).
The choice is made by LaunchServices from the document types the
installed applications declare.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-b bundle-id"
.It Fl a Ar application
Open with this application, given by name (looked up in
.Pa /Applications ,
.Pa /System/Applications
and
.Pa /System/Library/CoreServices )
or by path.
With no files, the application is launched or brought to the front.
.It Fl b Ar bundle-id
Open with the application with this bundle identifier.
.It Fl e , Fl t
Open with the text editor, Alcor.
.It Fl R , Fl -reveal
Show the files in Argos, each selected in a window on its folder,
instead of opening them.
.It Fl n
Start a new instance of the application even if one is running.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr launchctl 1
